      "evidence": "Verified npm tarball SHA-512, the annotated upstream v1.4.3 tag (commit equals npm gitHead) and publisher continuity (davidlehn for 1.4.1, 1.4.2 and 1.4.3). All 49 lib/ runtime modules match upstream source byte for byte; dist/*.min.js browser bundles and flash/ are outside this source-comparison scope and outside the listhen require path (main: lib/index.js). The v1.4.1..v1.4.3 lib diff only touches ed25519.js (small-order key rejection), http.js (linear header trim), tls.js (ServerHello compression check, no-session guard), x509.js (nameConstraints parsing and enforcement) and pem.js (String() coercion in decode); it adds no requires, I/O, eval or network calls. No install hooks. listhen uses only pki/rsa/md.sha256/asn1/PEM helpers for dev certificates. This review does not exempt vulnerabilities or Socket findings.",
